{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nconst ll LIM = LLONG_MAX - (ll)MOD * MOD;\ntypedef int Mat[32][32];\n\nvoid mmult(const Mat &A, const Mat &B, Mat &C, int n) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            ll cur = 0;\n            for (int k = 0; k < n; ++k) {\n                cur += (ll)A[i][k] * B[k][j];\n                if (cur > LIM) cur %= MOD;\n            }\n            C[i][j] = (int)(cur % MOD);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvoid mcopy(const Mat &A, Mat &B, int n) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n            B[i][j] = A[i][j];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ll n; int base;\n    scanf(\"%lld %d\", &n, &base);\n    int sz = base + 1;\n    static Mat mat[60][32];\n    for (int i = 0; i < base; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < sz; ++j)\n            for (int k = 0; k < sz; ++k)\n                mat[0][i][j][k] = (i == j || j == k) ? 1 : 0;\n    int ci = 0, cj = 0; ll step = 1;\n    while (step <= n / base) {\n        ++ci;\n        step *= base;\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i <= ci; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < base; ++j) {\n            for (int k = 0; k < sz; ++k)\n                for (int l = 0; l < sz; ++l)\n                    mat[i][j][k][l] = (k == l) ? 1 : 0;\n            for (int k = 0; k < base; ++k) {\n                Mat tmp;\n                mmult(mat[i][j], mat[i-1][(j+k)%base], tmp, sz);\n                mcopy(tmp, mat[i][j], sz);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    Mat have;\n    for (int k = 0; k < sz; ++k)\n        for (int l = 0; l < sz; ++l)\n            have[k][l] = (k == l) ? 1 : 0;\n    for (; ci >= 0; --ci, step /= base) {\n        int times = (int)((n / step) % base);\n        for (int x = 0; x < times; ++x) {\n            Mat tmp;\n            mmult(have, mat[ci][cj], tmp, sz);\n            mcopy(tmp, have, sz);\n            if (++cj >= base) cj -= base;\n        }\n    }\n    int ret = 0;\n    for (int k = 0; k < sz; ++k) {\n        ret += have[k][base];\n        if (ret >= MOD) ret -= MOD;\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", ret);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mmult(A, B, n):\n    C = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            cur = 0\n            for k in range(n):\n                cur += A[i][k] * B[k][j]\n            C[i][j] = cur % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef mcopy(A):\n    n = len(A)\n    return [row[:] for row in A]\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    base = int(data[1])\n    sz = base + 1\n\n    # mat[ci][j] is a sz x sz matrix\n    mat = []\n    # Initialize mat[0]\n    mat0 = []\n    for i in range(base):\n        m = [[0]*sz for _ in range(sz)]\n        for j in range(sz):\n            for k in range(sz):\n                m[j][k] = 1 if (i == j or j == k) else 0\n        mat0.append(m)\n    mat.append(mat0)\n\n    ci = 0\n    cj = 0\n    step = 1\n    while step <= n // base:\n        ci += 1\n        step *= base\n\n    for i in range(1, ci+1):\n        mat_i = []\n        for j in range(base):\n            # Initialize identity matrix\n            m = [[0]*sz for _ in range(sz)]\n            for k in range(sz):\n                m[k][k] = 1\n            for k in range(base):\n                tmp = mmult(m, mat[i-1][(j+k)%base], sz)\n                m = mcopy(tmp)\n            mat_i.append(m)\n        mat.append(mat_i)\n\n    # have matrix initially identity\n    have = [[0]*sz for _ in range(sz)]\n    for k in range(sz):\n        have[k][k] = 1\n\n    for ci_idx in range(ci, -1, -1):\n        times = (n // step) % base\n        for x in range(times):\n            tmp = mmult(have, mat[ci_idx][cj], sz)\n            have = mcopy(tmp)\n            cj += 1\n            if cj >= base:\n                cj -= base\n        step //= base\n\n    ret = 0\n    for k in range(sz):\n        ret += have[k][base]\n        if ret >= MOD:\n            ret -= MOD\n    print(ret)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.510157047363464e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0002766464895103127, -0.20372354984283447, -3.933898824470816e-06, -0.008626339957118034, -4.577531944960356e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.2278481335670222e-05, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -0.078900545835495, -0.002478862414136529, -0.0004463391669560224, -2.861018856492592e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -2.1576648578047752e-05, 0.0, -0.003185557434335351, -0.1274765133857727, -2.3364747903542593e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.29851406812667847, 0.0, -7.986990567587782e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.3869219422340393, -3.981510963058099e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07,